23934","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116221","id":4782423934,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHQ3_fg","user":{"login":"Nallebeorn","id":7013489,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMTM0ODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7013489?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn","html_url":"https://github.com/Nallebeorn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-23T18:49:54Z","updated_at":"2026-06-23T18:49:54Z","body":"> I think the original problem would be better resolved by making gizmos use a custom shader, which makes it possible to implement FOV-independent gizmos, but also a [semi-fixed size behavior](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/10018).\r\n\r\nAlright, this seems reasonable to me. The opinions I got in rocketchat was also that if the scale was to be configurable, it would make more sense for it to either follow the UI scale or for there to be some common scale setting for all gizmos, rather than a specific setting like this one, and that also makes sense.\r\n\r\nI'll leave this PR open though until it's actually superseded by a fix for the original FOV issue.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4782423934/react